WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.118
Before Ben can apply for jobs, he completes background screening in llama dot I D.

00:00:05.118 --> 00:00:10.298
Its approved-candidate signal reaches Edwina, making him eligible to be considered.

00:00:10.298 --> 00:00:14.042
Candidates awaiting approval cannot apply or receive offers.

00:00:15.242 --> 00:00:21.828
Helen, the school cover manager, uses WhatsApp on her phone to ask Edwin for a Year Six maths teacher.

00:00:21.828 --> 00:00:24.411
They need to arrive by eight forty-five.

00:00:24.411 --> 00:00:27.704
This illustrates the proposed WhatsApp integration.

00:00:28.904 --> 00:00:34.212
Helen’s message now appears in Sarah’s Edwina workspace, attached to the booking.

00:00:34.212 --> 00:00:36.833
Helen has not re-entered it in a portal.

00:00:36.833 --> 00:00:40.830
Edwina uses those requirements to find six potential matches.

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:46.749
Edwina first includes only candidates with current llama dot I D approval.

00:00:46.749 --> 00:00:52.169
It then checks relevant experience, availability and whether they can arrive on time.

00:00:52.169 --> 00:00:56.824
The shortlist is ranked using experience, previous MAT work and feedback.

00:00:58.024 --> 00:01:04.914
Ben sees the request on his Today page, alongside availability, timesheets, payroll setup and learning.

00:01:04.914 --> 00:01:07.657
The urgent assignment is the main action.

00:01:08.857 --> 00:01:11.689
Ben confirms he can arrive by eight forty-five.

00:01:11.689 --> 00:01:15.966
His reply can come through the app or the proposed WhatsApp connection.

00:01:15.966 --> 00:01:20.003
An available calendar is not assumed to mean he is ready to travel.

00:01:21.203 --> 00:01:25.769
Sarah can now see Ben’s readiness, response time and expected arrival.

00:01:25.769 --> 00:01:31.771
His experience and previous MAT work remain visible beside one clear action: send the offer.

00:01:32.971 --> 00:01:37.625
Ben reviews the school, pay, working hours and arrival instructions.

00:01:37.625 --> 00:01:40.432
He acknowledges the briefing and accepts.

00:01:40.432 --> 00:01:42.759
Everyone follows the same booking.

00:01:43.959 --> 00:01:45.016
Ben has accepted.

00:01:45.016 --> 00:01:50.925
His existing approval is rechecked, and the proposed Bullhorn connection records the placement.

00:01:50.925 --> 00:01:57.020
This records the booking; background screening was completed before Ben entered the matching pool.

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:03.139
The school sees Ben confirmed, his expected arrival and a link to the booking.

00:02:03.139 --> 00:02:07.554
Helen can focus on welcoming the educator rather than chasing updates.

00:02:08.754 --> 00:02:12.091
Helen messages Ben with reception instructions.

00:02:12.091 --> 00:02:14.932
He receives them against the assignment.

00:02:14.932 --> 00:02:17.488
She can also contact Sarah at Edwin.

00:02:18.688 --> 00:02:25.929
Candidates can also browse recommended jobs, compare dates, pay and journey information, and register interest.

00:02:25.929 --> 00:02:30.494
Their schedule, pay records and learning remain part of the wider app.

00:02:31.694 --> 00:02:35.330
For a separate booking, Edwin asks BrightPath for cover.

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:39.161
Olivia submits an available educator and the evidence pack.

00:02:39.161 --> 00:02:43.056
Edwin reviews the proposal and remains the school’s contact.

00:02:44.256 --> 00:02:51.796
Rachel’s trust dashboard brings together spend against budget, fill rates, time to fill, open cover and school comparisons.

00:02:51.796 --> 00:02:57.497
She can move from an organisation-wide view into the schools and records that need attention.

00:02:58.697 --> 00:03:05.118
Rachel can explore spend by month, role and school, reasons for cover, timesheets and assurance.

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:09.466
Charts reveal trends; school and date filters define each report.

00:03:10.666 --> 00:03:14.312
Rachel selects spend by job role for the chosen period.

00:03:14.312 --> 00:03:20.741
She can create a PDF to circulate or export the filtered figures into Excel for further analysis.

00:03:21.941 --> 00:03:31.622
This is the report produced by the prototype’s PDF generator: the selected dates, school scope, role totals and definitions travel with the data.

00:03:31.622 --> 00:03:35.360
The Excel export preserves numeric amounts for analysis.

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:43.292
The term outlook shows when cover demand may rise, with actual observations separated from the forecast scenario.

00:03:43.292 --> 00:03:47.819
Rachel can inspect the weekly values and planning assumptions before acting.

00:03:49.019 --> 00:03:55.304
The monthly cost view combines worked spend, confirmed future cover and an allowance for further demand.

00:03:55.304 --> 00:04:01.287
It shows a central scenario and range, helping the trust discuss likely budget pressure with Edwin.
